::PC_U04_L04_GP_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U04_L04_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.6
Question:
Which comparison is needed to identify the major axis of an ellipse in item.
{
~A. Compare only the signs between the terms#This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
=B. Compare the denominators under the squared terms#Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
~C. Use the smaller denominator as the full major axis length#This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~D. Treat both axes as asymptotes#This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
}

